# Database

- Every schema change is a new timestamped migration; never edit an applied migration.
- Prefer additive/backward-compatible migrations. Document rollback or forward-fix in `docs/MIGRATIONS.md`.
- Enable RLS on every exposed table and test exact policies with pgTAP.
- Enforce critical invariants in PostgreSQL, not only in UI/API validation.
- All writes set actor identity and are covered by audit triggers.
- Storage buckets remain private; validate MIME, size, path ownership, and role on both API and policy layers.
- Run `pnpm db:reset`, `pnpm db:test`, and regenerate types after migration changes.
